      "prompt_texts": {
        "3f611e71f2648528027bbe2d3b376ebb4a9f1f537626f17fb5f3c67e31943e77": "# nu - prompt 001\n\n<!-- recorded: 2026-11-12T20:10:17Z; source: agent -->\n\nDemonstration prompt, written by the implementing agent (Claude) to exercise the studio; it is not a prompt from Michael Gogins.\n\nCompose a very short study called nu, about 18 seconds long: a slow, bell-like melody in D Dorian over a low drone, with reverberation. Write it directly as one complete Csound .csd file, with the instruments and the notes, using the studio p-field conventions (p4 MIDI key, p5 MIDI velocity, p6 depth, p7 pan).\n",
        "5c5273f69ec837bdc84a957e5d84992cc71da06bc659dab82ec446901be92967": "# nu - prompt 002\n\n<!-- recorded: 2026-11-12T20:11:13Z; source: agent -->\n\nDemonstration prompt, written by the implementing agent (Claude) to exercise the studio; it is not a prompt from Michael Gogins.\n\nKeep the instruments of nu exactly as they are, but stop writing the notes by hand. Generate the score with a Python program that uses CsoundAC: the bells play a seeded random walk on the D Dorian scale with irregular rhythm, moving between left and right; the drone on D is joined by its fifth halfway through. Keep the program beside the piece so that the .csd can be regenerated from it, and record the random seed.\n",
        "70921141ba13af23f9c5b36510ff981fb186c1aa2a476cd377248877ac3d7be3": "# nu - prompt 003\n\n<!-- recorded: 2026-11-12T20:12:08Z; source: agent -->\n\nDemonstration prompt, written by the implementing agent (Claude) to exercise the studio; it is not a prompt from Michael Gogins.\n\nRevise the generator. Answer the bell melody with a canon: the same melody four scale steps higher (a diatonic fifth, staying in D Dorian), two seconds later, softer, farther away, and on the opposite side. Let the melody range more widely than before. Make the drone a little softer so the two bell voices stay clear.\n"
      },
